Z||000015||mbramble||03-11-2000||09:23 AM||||Hey ChadMan,<P>Except for the year, you are talking about my car.  It's an '87 -- very basic -- coupe wth a 2.5L that I 'inherited' from my son when he went into the Navy and bought a new car.  He inherited it from his sister when she married and moved away.  She bought it in '94.  The paint was 'orange-peeled' all over the top and rear deck and he did some sanding/priming.  When I got it, it ran like absolute crap and it was determined it had a bad ignition coil.  Had that replaced, replaced the bad auto transmission gasket so it stopped leaking, and made some minor repairs and now I drive it to work everyday.  Love it!  I hate when I finally convince myself that I need to drive my truck some to keep the battery charged, etc.  I just installed an amp (had put in a nice am/fm/cassette for my daughter the first Christmas she had it), and have a CD changer in the mail. I will replace the speakers, install a wing (used, $52 from e-bay!), have it repainted, and do a little work in the interior.  I am as happy with mine as you guys are with your really, realyy, really nice cars!!!||||reg||1
Z||000016||sully5||03-11-2000||02:38 PM||||I just got my first Fiero a couple of weeks ago - a 1986 SE. Looks a lot like batboys 85 GT, 'cept mine has the black ground effects instead of silver. Took it out last night for the first time since I did the brakes. I had driven them before, but forgot how fun they are. Don't see too many of them around here anymore, unfortunately.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||14
